  "prose": [
    {
      "title": null,
      "text": "The KBD (Keyboard) component can be used to indicate a textual user input from the keyboard inside other elements such as in text, tables, cards, and more.\n\nUse the semantic `<Kbd>` keyboard input tag to use the default monospace font which is best suited for representing input keys.\n\nTo start using the `<Kbd>` component you need to import it from `flowbite-react`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Default KBD",
      "text": "Here's a list of KBD components that you can use inside any other element.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "KBD inside text",
      "text": "Use this example by nesting an inline KBD component inside a paragraph.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "KBD inside table",
      "text": "The KBD component can also be used inside table components to denote what type of key can be pressed for certain descriptions.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Arrow keys",
      "text": "Use this example to show arrow keys inside the KBD styled element.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Letter Keys",
      "text": "Use this example to show arrow keys inside the KBD styled element.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Number Keys",
      "text": "Use this example to show a key inside a KBD component from the english numeral system.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Function keys",
      "text": "This example can be used to denote function keys inside the KBD component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
